  "verbalization": "Nortriptyline is linked to the Sodium/Potassium Transporting ATPase subunits through a chain of side effects involving dopamine. The drug's side effect of QRS complex, which is associated with dopamine, directly targets these subunits. This suggests a potential mechanism where nortriptyline influences dopamine signaling, which in turn affects the activity of the Sodium/Potassium Transporting ATPase subunits. The evidence from both paths supports a causal relationship, though the exact nature of the interaction remains unclear. The integration of these findings highlights a possible role in modulating ion transport, potentially through dopamine-mediated pathways.",
